//
// PROBE: F222 — a method slot holding a PTR that names no method.
//
// `ptr` makes a PTR from a string without calling it, so a class may carry one
// whose name nothing registers. Dispatch finds the slot, and the reference
// refuses the call with `VM Method <name> not registered`, naming the method
// and not the slot (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/multistackvm_object.rs:71).
// Bund2 once said `m(<slot>) returned: method <name> not registered`.
//
// The program ends in that refusal, so the stack the capture dumps is what was
// left when it was made.

:P class :.super [ :Object ] set :m "nosuch" ptr set register
"probe: a PTR slot naming no method" println
:m :P object !
